/* =====================================================================================================
   SPARE PART 3D MODELS AND SHEETS (owner: Claude B)  Schematic, generated from the part description, SYNTHETIC geometry.
   Every material of the baseline data has an item type (53 types). spiPartModel(description) parses the text (size, rating, schedule,
   dimensions, material) and builds the solids with the same renderer as the equipment models (g3d.js). Where the text carries a real size
   (bearing designation, NPS and class, O-ring ID and cross-section, stud size, firebrick dimensions, thermocouple diameter and length)
   the solid is sized from it; where it carries only a type code (MODEL XY123) typical proportions are used and the sheet says so.
   Standards named for what they cover: ISO 15 (rolling bearings), ASME B16.5 (flanges), B16.20 and B16.21 (gaskets), B36.10M (pipe),
   B16.9 and B16.11 (fittings), ISO 3601 (O-rings), ASME B18.2.2 and ASTM A193, A194 (stud bolts, nuts), API 682 (seals), API 610 (impellers,
   wear rings), API 612 (blades, journal and thrust bearings), IEC 60534 and ISA-75 (valve trim), ISA-5.1 (instruments).
   Functions: spiPartParse, spiPartModel, spiPart3D (viewer html), spiPartSheet (2D sheet svg), spiPartThumb (small svg).
   ===================================================================================================== */
